                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f85552f-4913-314a-bc64-27d2805816f8",
                                        "entry_id": "16542dda-aed2-3b7a-8341-9a7f91b9fd99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Russian communist revolutionary, a member of the Bolshevik Party in the Communist Revolution of Russia in 1917."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0562e52-208c-461c-be0a-902d9f06bff8",
                                                "sense_id": "9f85552f-4913-314a-bc64-27d2805816f8",
                                                "text": "Мы, большевики, утверждаем, что на нашей стороне большинство настоящих, русских, партийных деятелей.",
                                                "translation": "Vladimir Lenin",
                                                "english": "Vladimir Lenin"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4c72643-4dcc-4bd5-8f36-1643872eba6c",
                                                "sense_id": "9f85552f-4913-314a-bc64-27d2805816f8",
                                                "text": "But such points were on the whole lost in the picture as it appeared in gross: everyone had confessed, the Old Bolsheviks had publicly avowed disgraceful plans and actions. The whole business almost passed belief. Were the confessions true? How had they been obtained? What did it all signify? We are told that the confessions were as little believed in Russia as abroad, ‘or even less’, but that the average Soviet citizen who had not been in jail found them as puzzling as foreigners did."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f543ef5c-6d6b-3689-865d-72a6fe8b440b",
                                        "entry_id": "16542dda-aed2-3b7a-8341-9a7f91b9fd99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the Communist Party that ruled the Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic and the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
